C03: a request that stops on an article or preposition arrived cut; the turn says where and asks how it continues (FILES1591)

H0426 «Crea un archivo en mi escritorio llamado carter_test.txt que contenga la fecha actual, el nombre del» resolved to a text-file write whose content ends mid-phrase; writing it would have invented the rest or produced an incomplete file. Under the owner's rule for cut messages (understand from context or ask), `cut_request_tail` names the input kind `cut_request` when a request of six or more words ends, without closing punctuation, on an article, preposition or conjunction, and `clarify_unresolved_input` composes one short question that says the message arrived cut at those last words and asks how it continues, doing nothing yet and never completing the request on its own (one corrected retry). Screened over the whole private registry: only H0426 takes the new kind.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


